PianoIR is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE): piano's IR transmitter (owner item HW-IR, 2026-11-24). What it
takes from other work, and from where:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoTouch/GeniSpi.c / GeniSpi.h (sha256 2042cfc9647391e24d5a558202046425ac62a05adfc73afe769367b8374e3f91 / e73891e4571c5323bca27aaf987bafa002856dfa1dcee156ff31b119e2d3ae3c):
    compiled in, not copied (the GENI SPI engine: SE DMA, the loopback, the clock divider).
  package/PianoDwc3/SmmuStream.h (sha256 8f566938f259730d15407aa2d84abb3f6ec3b06c7bf3dabaef78c7e7fbb930a3): included, not copied (the bypass bank for
    stream 0x423).
  package/PianoTouch/PianoTouch.cpp: the SE bring-up order (votes under PianoA830's lock word, the branch check before every engine
    access, the contiguous DMA buffer kept to the end, the cache maintenance, the SMMU on the matching thread), re-written here.
  package/PianoTorch/PianoTorch.cpp, tooling/native/piano-torch/piano-torch.c: the kext's shape (probe gate on the boot argument,
    the stage word, an administrator-only setProperties) and the tool's form, re-written.
  package/PianoBluetooth/BtHw.h: the QUP2 vote word and RCG/DFS layout (facts), re-expressed for the s7 engine in IrHw.h.
  package/include/PianoPowerContract.h: the power-tree join.

Facts only (no code or text copied):
  The Linux piano kernel yzddmr6/linux-sm8750-piano 1c21cb9895d69c1c5e83ceae68952fedf522644a (GPL-2.0; pinned by
  yzddmr6/xiaomipad-8pro-mainline a43f79c): sm8750-xiaomi-piano-desktop.dts (spi15, "xiaomi,piano-ir-spi", the pin states),
  sm8750.dtsi (spi@89c000, geniqup@8c0000 and its stream, the pins), gcc-sm8750.c (the s7 branch, RCG and votes),
  pinctrl-sm8750.c (gpio28-31 function 1), drivers/media/rc/ir-spi.c (the piano variant's waveform rules: sample rate, carrier
  period, duty, cumulative boundaries, the trailing zero word, the 32 KiB bound). IrWave.h re-implements that behaviour.
  Project-SunUEFI 766ab7ca35d1 (linux/dts/piano-ir-spi-controller.dtso, patches/linux/7.3/0043): GPIO29 active high, idle low,
  park only after the engine is idle.
  The NEC code timings (9 ms / 4.5 ms leader, 562.5 us units, 108 ms repeat): the public protocol description.
No vendor firmware, no Apple binary or payload.
